## SpacetimeDB Type Generation

**NEVER** manually create types for database entities. Types are auto-generated from the Rust schema.

After any schema changes in `server/src/lib.rs`, regenerate bindings:
```bash
pnpm generate
# or: spacetime generate --lang typescript --out-dir src/module_bindings --project-path server
```

## Key Patterns

**Connection & Identity:**
```typescript
const { conn, identity, connected } = useSpacetimeDB();
```

**Read Data:**
```typescript
const users = () => conn()?.db.user.getAll() ?? [];
const myUser = () => conn()?.db.user.identity.find(identity());
```

**Call Reducers (mutations):**
```typescript
conn()?.reducers.sendChatMessage(roomId, content, null);
```

**Subscribe to Updates:**
```typescript
conn()?.db.user.onInsert((ctx, user) => { /* handle */ });
conn()?.db.user.onUpdate((ctx, oldUser, newUser) => { /* handle */ });
```

## Module Bindings

Files in `src/module_bindings/` are **auto-generated** - never edit manually.

See [SpacetimeDB Docs](https://spacetimedb.com/docs/sdks/typescript/quickstart) and `SPACETIMEDB_EXAMPLES.tsx` for more patterns.
